---
name: dev-sanity-bead
version: 0.1.0
description: The sanity check bead that follows a sprint's dev bead. It is blocked by the dev bead; dev beads that require this sprint list this bead in their `blocked_by`. Recipient and message are in resources/dev-sanity.md. Render strictly, then `jq -c .` into the import JSONL.
format: json
required_variables:
  - id
  - parent
  - dev_bead
  - phase
  - sprint
  - stack
  - assignee
optional_variables:
  - priority
defaults:
  priority: 2
---
{
  "id": {{ id | tojson }},
  "title": {{ (sprint ~ ": sanity check") | tojson }},
  "issue_type": "task",
  "status": "open",
  "priority": {{ priority }},
  "assignee": {{ assignee | tojson }},
  "description": {{ ("Sanity check of " ~ dev_bead ~ " (sprint " ~ sprint ~ ").\n\nVerify that the work is done:\n\n- the agent did not skip anything;\n- there are no obvious errors;\n- lint passes.\n\nThis is not QA.") | tojson }},
  "acceptance_criteria": {{ ("- [ ] every deliverable and acceptance criterion of " ~ dev_bead ~ " is present in the pushed head (workflow steps that come after the sanity check, such as linking and QA, are not judged)\n- [ ] no obvious errors\n- [ ] lint passes") | tojson }},
  "labels": {{ ["phase-" ~ phase, "stage:dev-sanity", "stack:" ~ stack] | tojson }},
  "dependencies": [
    {"issue_id": {{ id | tojson }}, "depends_on_id": {{ parent | tojson }}, "type": "parent-child"},
    {"issue_id": {{ id | tojson }}, "depends_on_id": {{ dev_bead | tojson }}, "type": "blocks"}
  ],
  "metadata": {
    "phase": {{ phase | tojson }},
    "sprint": {{ sprint | tojson }},
    "stack": {{ stack | tojson }},
    "dev_bead": {{ dev_bead | tojson }}
  }
}
